Feature: slide-fixes
Target module: core ($$.sm(el).slide)

- .vSlide.pos now transitions right and bottom as well as left and top, so positionProperty:
  "right" slides instead of jumping.
- slide.toRight honours positionProperty (it hard-coded left).
- slide.toRight applies the same defaults as toLeft (use, positions, dimensions,
  positionProperty); with use omitted it used to throw a TypeError.
- slide.toRight with use: "dimension" and no end width opens to scrollWidth instead of
  throwing a ReferenceError on an undeclared `width`.
- slide.toLeft / toRight choose the CSS class after defaulting use, so an omitted use gets
  .vSlide.dim like an explicit "dimension" (it got .vSlide.pos and the width didn't animate).

- Position slides (toLeft / toRight) jump to positions.x[0] with transitions off, then
  animate to x[1]. Before, an element not already at x[0] (one just unhidden) animated toward
  x[0] and was turned straight back, so a slide-in appeared without moving.

Why: app.myinvitees.com slides its right-anchored My quota panel with positionProperty:
"right". It needed an app-side CSS override for the transition, and used toLeft for both
directions because toRight ignored positionProperty.

Verified: the slide object was cut out of the core and run in Node against a stub element,
before and after the change. Before: toRight with positionProperty "right" moved left, and
use omitted / no end width threw TypeError / ReferenceError. toLeft with use omitted got the
pos class. After: right moves -340 -> 0 and 0 -> -340, toRight without positionProperty
still moves left, use omitted runs the dimension branch with the dim class, and no end width
opens to scrollWidth. Start-position fix verified in headless Chromium in real time (over the DevTools protocol)
with the card tool's sequence (unhide, read offsetWidth, slide right -340 -> 0, close, reopen).
Before: both opens sat at the open position from the first frame, and only the close moved.
After: open, close and reopen all move across the 500ms. (Virtual-time headless runs showed
later transitions frozen, an artifact of virtual time and not of the code.)

Affected projects: app.myinvitees.com is the only caller of slide in VilsHub, and it passes
use explicitly. Behaviour changes only for calls that omit use, call toRight with
positionProperty "right", or slide by right/bottom. Calls that pass use, and toRight calls
without positionProperty, behave as before. dist/ (git-ignored) is rebuilt by ./minify.sh.
